<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰν-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>intoxicate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνῶσαι σῶμα ποτοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Critias
					6.28D.
				</span></i>
			 : elsewh. always 
				Pass.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνόομαι</span></b> , <i>get drunk,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνωθέντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.292
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				16.5
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνωθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					929
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				2.411.14
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνοῦσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.672a
				</span></i>
			 : fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνωθήσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Stoic.</u>
					3.163
				</span></i>
			 : mostly in pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠνωμένος,</span>
			
				Ion.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.18
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγαν ᾠνωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					409
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείπνοις, ἡνίκ᾽ ἦν ᾠνωμένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					268
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾠνωμένας κρατῆρι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					687
				</span></i>
			 : codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i> always give <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰνωμένος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>EN</u>
				1147a14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1152a15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1154b10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1389a19
			</span></i>. (The word used in good 
				Att.
			 Prose is <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεθύω</span> (q. v.) ;
			but in <u>Stoic.</u>l.c. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰ.</span>
			=
			<i>drink wine in moderation,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεθυσθῆναι,</span>
			<i>to be the worse for wine.</i>) </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>turn into wine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				11.517
			</span></i>.</div>
